          %title Decidable propositions
          %h1#decidable_propositions Decidable propositions
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#ExternalDecidability"} Externally decidable propositions in logic
              %li
                %a{:href => "#InternalDecidability"} Internally decidable propositions in constructive mathematics
              %li
                %a{:href => "#relation_between_these"} Relation between these
              %li
                %a{:href => "#categorial_interpretation"} Categorial interpretation
              %li
                %a{:href => "#in_dependent_type_theory"}  In dependent type theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"}  Related concepts
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            is decidable if we know whether it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/false"} false
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#ExternalDecidability"}> External decidability
                \: either
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \not p
                may be
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deduction"} deduced
                in the theory. This is a statement in the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metalanguage"} metalanguage
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InternalDecidability"}> Internal decidability
                \:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∨
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \vee \not p
                may be deduced in the theory; in other words “
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                or not
                = succeed "\u201D" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+language"} object language
          %p
            There are another two interpretations, which interpret “or” as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exclusive+disjunction"} exclusive disjunction
            rather than inclusive
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#ExternalDecidability"}> External decidability
                \: that exactly one of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \not p
                holds may be
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deduction"} deduced
                in the theory. This is a statement in the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metalanguage"} metalanguage
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InternalDecidability"}> Internal decidability
                \:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %munder
                        %mo ∨
                        %mo ̲
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \underline{\vee} \not p
                may be deduced in the theory; in other words “exactly one of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                or not
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                holds” holds in the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+language"} object language
          %p
            The versions using exclusive disjunction are equivalent to the versions using inclusive disjunction. This is because
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            implies its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation"} double negation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            or not
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            or not not
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            or not
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            implies that “(
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            or not
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            or not not
            = succeed ")\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exclusive+disjunction"} exclusive disjunction
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
          %h2#ExternalDecidability Externally decidable propositions in logic
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic"} logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            in a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            (or in a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            of a given theory) is
            %strong externally decidable
            if there is in that theory (or in that context) a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            or a refutation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            (a proof of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg{p}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
          %p
            Any statement that can be proved or refuted is decidable, and one might hope for a consistent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundation+of+mathematics"} foundation of mathematics
            in which every statement is decidable. However, Gödel's
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/incompleteness+theorem"} incompleteness theorem
            dashes these hopes; any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/consistent+theory"} consistent theory
            strong enough to model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic"} arithmetic
            (actually a rather weak form of arithmetic) must contain undecidable statements.
          %p
            For example, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum+hypothesis"} continuum hypothesis
            is undecidable in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ZFC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ZFC
            is consistent at all.
          %h2#InternalDecidability Internally decidable propositions in constructive mathematics
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is
            %strong internally decidable
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+excluded+middle"} law of excluded middle
            applies to
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \vee \neg{p}
            holds. Of course, in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg{(p \vee \neg{p})}
            is always false, but this is not enough to guarantee that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \vee \neg{p}
            is true.
          %p
            For example, consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+hypothesis"} Riemann hypothesis
            (or any of the many unsolved
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1
            %span.newWikiWord
              propositions
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Pi-1-proposition"} ?
            in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x, P(x)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate"} predicate
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(x)
            is decidable (that is,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ¬
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x, P(x) \vee \neg{P(x)}
            holds), and indeed one can in principle work out which with pencil and paper. However, the Riemann hypothesis itself has not yet been proved (constructively) to be decidable.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            has
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+equality"} decidable equality
            if every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equation
            between elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (every proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
            in
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            of a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+subset"} decidable subset
            if every statement of membership in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            (every proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in B
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h2#relation_between_these Relation between these
          %p
            In many foundations of constructive mathematics, the
            %span.newWikiWord
              disjunction property
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/disjunction+property"} ?
            holds (in the global context). That is, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \vee q
            can be proved, then either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            can be proved or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            can be proved. By Gödel's incompleteness theorem, no consistent foundation of classical arithmetic can have this property, but some consistent foundations of intuitionistic arithmetic (such as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+arithmetic"} Heyting arithmetic
          %p
            In any consistent logic with the disjunction property, a proposition is externally decidable if and only if it can be proved to be internally decidable. (Note that the claim that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is externally decidable is a statement in the metalanguage, while the claim that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is internally decidable is a statement in the object language.)
          %h2#categorial_interpretation Categorial interpretation
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+logic"} first-order
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic logic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+contexts"} category of contexts
            which is a Heyting category.
          %p
            Under this correspondence, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contexts"} contexts
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            correspond to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            in a given context correspond to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            of that object. Then a proposition in a context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is externally decidable if and only if it is, as a subobject of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            itself (corresponding to being provable) or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            (corresponding to being refutable). And a proposition in the context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is internally decidable if and only if, when thought of as a subobject
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg{A}
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-valued+category"} two-valued
            if and only if the context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is consistent and every proposition in that context is externally decidable.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+category"} Boolean category
            if and only if every proposition in every context is internally decidable.
          .query
            %p
              This makes me think that we should define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              to be externally decidable iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is provable whenever it is not refutable, which in a constructive metalogic is weaker than the definition above. But then we lose the relationship with the disjunction property. I guess that we need intuitionistic, classical, and paraconsistent forms of external decidability, just as for two-valuedness.
          %h2#in_dependent_type_theory  In dependent type theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} mere proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            which comes with an element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lem
                      %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{lem}_P:P \vee \neg P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi B
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \vee B \coloneqq [A + B]
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
            of two types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg A \coloneqq A \to \emptyset
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            of type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A + B
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum+type"} sum type
            of types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+truncation"} propositional truncation
            of type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isDecidable
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isDecidable}(P) \coloneqq \mathrm{isProp}(P) \times (P \vee \neg P)
          %h2#related_concepts  Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+decidable+propositions"} type of decidable propositions
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+subsingleton"} decidable subsingleton
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-decidable+proposition"} semi-decidable proposition
